{
  "_readme": [
    "One entry per model id. Fields:",
    "  backend : openai | openrouter | custom   (which code path in client.py)",
    "  kind    : chat | reasoning               (reasoning => no temperature, large output cap)",
    "  reasoning / provider : OpenRouter only   (explicit effort=medium; first-party host pinned)",
    "",
    "TO ADD A NEW MODEL, append one line, e.g.",
    "  OpenAI, native or OpenAI-compatible gateway :  \"gpt-6\": {\"backend\": \"openai\", \"kind\": \"reasoning\"}",
    "  non-OpenAI via OpenRouter                    :  \"vendor/model\": {\"backend\": \"openrouter\", \"kind\": \"reasoning\", \"reasoning\": {\"effort\": \"medium\"}, \"provider\": \"<FirstPartyHost>\"}",
    "  anything via your own API (custom_client.py) :  \"my-model\": {\"backend\": \"custom\", \"kind\": \"reasoning\"}",
    "An OpenAI-style name that is missing here still works on the openai backend (kind inferred from the name).",
    "",
    "The judge is gpt-4.1 and is frozen. It must be reachable through whichever backend you use."
  ],
